    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "Sep 24, 2026"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "When Intelligence Becomes Abundant, Judgement Becomes Scarce"
    },
    {
     "t": "p",
     "text": "I sometimes miss the days of poorly formatted Word documents, clumsy PowerPoint decks and emails with typos and imperfect grammar. Those imperfections made the person behind the work visible. You could see where someone had wrestled with an idea, where they were uncertain and how they had arrived at a conclusion. When you challenged an assumption, there was usually a human train of thought to examine."
    },
